      "The eight languages in steam/localization/languages.json exactly match the packaged data/lang/index.js. Expansion work directories were not treated as shipped content.",
      "Titles and requested UI terms match the original GameContent catalogs for every translated shipped locale.",
      "The packaged metadata reports 273 UI entries per translated locale, while each actual packaged catalog contains 189. Original metadata and catalogs report 279. Metadata counts are therefore not used as the authoritative terminology source.",
      "Each original catalog has 90 keys absent from the packaged base catalog. The content builder explicitly moves walkthrough strings into DLC depots; this audit does not assume that every original-only key is a walkthrough string. No shared UI values differ.",
      "Labels are outputs of the packaged localization runtime in an isolated context with a stub locale preference and no DOM event execution: LarryI18n.t handles UI labels; localizeXML handles the three story menu options using catalog.story and punctuate. No browser, real localStorage, game saves or game files were modified. CJK punctuation normalization is recorded separately.",
      "directStart, listenStory and gameInfo are story-option labels, not catalog.ui entries. Calling LarryI18n.t alone would leave their Traditional Chinese source text untranslated. utility.js loads the scenario through LarryI18n.localizeXML; the terms here follow that actual story translation path."
